Chips in place of the focused window's title, drawn like the status
blocks: a window's _DWM_CHIPS property holds tab-separated "kind|text"
chips, and each is drawn as its kind's icon on the kind's colour
(chipkinds in config.h), then its text in SchemeChip. A kind config.h
doesn't know is skipped, and a window without the property shows its
title as before. dwm-chips (dwm/chips.sh) publishes a terminal's: its
directory, its git branch and status, and an agent's state. Applies after
chadwmbar.diff.

